Here’s a simple JSON query you can run against your index (replace `your_index_name` with the actual index):

```json
GET /your_index_name/_search
{
  "query": {
    "range": {
      "age": {
        "gte": 30,   // inclusive of 30
        "lt": 40     // exclusive of 40
      }
    }
  }
}
```

If you’re using the Java client, it would look something like this:

```java
SearchSourceBuilder sourceBuilder = new SearchSourceBuilder();
sourceBuilder.query(QueryBuilders.rangeQuery("age")
                                 .gte(30)
                                 .lt(40));
```

That will return all documents where the `age` field is between 30 (inclusive) and 40 (exclusive).
